dy  lots of public genomics data sets that  you can explore today on the queries  such as the 1000 genome platinum genomes  or the public accent portion a public  access portion of the TCGA there is also  multiple non-human variant data such as  the genomics cannabis or the rice 3k  which has variants that are called using  deep variants the other key advantage to  having the data in bigquery is how easy  it is to create cohorts and datasets  that can be used in sensor flow or other  machine learning frameworks easily and  and you can take advantage of they are  platform tools such as they are  notebooks to interact with your variant  data using Python or are very easily so  color is one of our customers who did  just that there is a very interesting  blog post on our website on how they  used variants transform and bigquery to  create machine learning models that beat  standard industry models in just weeks  so one of the reasons many have chosen  Google cloud for the genomics workloads  is that we don't just provide  infrastructure our product and  engineering teams have developed a  number of services and api's that cater  to the needs of healthcare and life  sciences community such as the  healthcare API that supports health  records in fire and hl7 format or the  imaging API to interact with DICOM the  life sciences API was developed to  enable workflow engines to take  advantage of Google Cloud in large scale  this is a reference architecture for  running workflows at scale and GCP raw  data from sequencers or other sources  typically would be uploaded to Google  Cloud storage and the workflow engine  would drawn on a Google compute engine  or in your own infrastructure or machine  and then would make rest calls to the  life sciences API the life sciences API  takes care of the full lifecycle of each  step in the pipeline from creating a  virtual machine with exactly the number  of cores  memories specified localizing the input  files and copying them from sto